  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "In 2026, Mother's Day (or Mothering Sunday) in the UK is celebrated on Sunday, March 15. Unlike the US date, the UK holiday falls on the fourth Sunday of Lent. It is a traditional day honoring mothers and mother figures with flowers, cards, and family meals. 2026 Date: March 15 2027 Date: March 7 Origins: Originally a medieval Christian tradition where people visited their \"mother church\" (the main church in their area) during Lent. Modern Day: It has evolved into a secular celebration similar to the US, often called \"Mother's Day,\" says Time and Date. Common Traditions: Giving gifts (flowers, chocolates), hosting afternoon teas, and families getting together to \"spoil\" mothers, says English Heritage. It is important to note that the date shifts every year based on the church calendar, according to Wikipedia.",
